# Line endings are pinned to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this the tree's endings are whatever each contributor's core.autocrlf
# happens to be, and a Windows checkout hands the hook a different file than a
# Linux one at the same commit. The hooks are shipped source — Claude Code runs
# them from the checkout — so "different bytes" is not cosmetic there.
#
# eol=lf, not merely text=auto: text=auto alone normalises the INDEX and lets
# autocrlf write CRLF back into the working tree. The explicit per-extension
# lines below say the same thing again for the files this repo is made of, so a
# future `-text` or `binary` rule cannot quietly take one of them with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.ico binary
